Mr. Rawls,
   I have worked with BBS-PC! for several years, and saw it grow from it's
4.13 version to it's current (almost 2 years old now) 4.20 version. At the
time it was the most stable program on the market. It is still concidered the
most stable in some areas of it's application.

   You - as a representative of Micro-System's Software - must recognize the
public (your end-users) as the potential customers for upgrades to any of your
software (Why else would you have recently updated Excellence!). They are the
people who invariably create the revenue that in turn pays your salary.

   For 1.5 years you (Micro-Systems Software) have been listening to hundreds
of sysop's desperatly asking/pleading for an update to BBS-PC. Due to the
complete lack of positive responce the majority of those 'potential' users
have looked to other software to accomplish what they want to do (run a BBS,
with the abilities currently un-available in BBS-PC). I could list two dozen
myself if I wanted to.

   I myself, am BETA testing come new software called Dialog.

   I honestly believe that by the time you 'find the time' to produce an
upgrade to BBS-PC, you simply will not have sales to support it. You cannot
thank anyone but yourselves for such action.
